          "title": "You'll want to know: paedagōgus, paedagōgī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paedagōgus, paedagōgī — \"a slave who takes a boy to school; a tutor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Paedagōgus puerum ad scholam dūcit. The slave-tutor takes the boy to school."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paedagōgus, paedagōgī m., borrowed from Greek paidagōgos, child-leader. English pedagogue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paedagōgus was borrowed from Greek paidagōgos \"child-leader\" (EtymDB), built from pais \"a child\" and agōgos \"leading\". English pedagogue comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
